n>During the pandemic, I got really into two hobbies -- writing code, and making cocktails. This project was one of the first web apps I built from scratch. We would host cocktail parties and I would send everyone this link and then they would order drinks from me at my &quot;bar&quot;. It was a lot of fun.</description><pubDate>Mon, 09 Jan 2023 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Go Portfolio</title><link>https://dominicgerman.github.io/posts/projects/gofolio/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://dominicgerman.github.io/posts/projects/gofolio/</guid><description>In 2024, I got really interested in backend web development -- REST APIs, databases, microservices, etc. During that period, I rebuilt my website using Go. It was a completely over-engineered web app with a SQL db, user auth, session management, form submissions... all implemented from scratch using only Go&apos;s standard library. Even the UI was written with Go&apos;s templating package. I&apos;m still in love with Go and its whole philosophy around software.</description><pubDate>Thu, 09 Jan 2025 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Homelab</title><link>https://dominicgerman.github.io/posts/projects/homelab/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://dominicgerman.github.io/posts/projects/homelab/</guid><description>My current obsession is homelabbing -- it&apos;s my favorite hands-on way of learning about technology. I&apos;m particularly interested in DevOps tech as it bridges my two worlds of software development and IT/operations.</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Jan 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Mount Prospect Web Design</title><link>https://dominicgerman.github.io/posts/projects/mpwd/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://dominicgerman.github.io/posts/projects/mpwd/</guid><description>In 2023, my wife and I started a small web design/development business. This was before we had kids -- we&apos;re a little busier these days. During that period, I went down the frontend web dev rabbit hole and we built several sites for clients that I still maintain today. I built our marketing site with Svelte and Tailwind and it was a very pleasant experience.</description><pubDate>Tue, 09 Jan 2024 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item></channel></rss>